# Multi-Region Support Implementation

## Overview
The Choreo CLI supports multiple deployment regions (US and EU) with region-specific configurations and token management.

## Core Components

### Region Management
- [internal/region/config.go](mdc:internal/region/config.go): Core region configuration and management
- [internal/cmd/region/cmd.go](mdc:internal/cmd/region/cmd.go): CLI command for region operations

### Configuration Structure
- [internal/config/types.go](mdc:internal/config/types.go): Common configuration types
- [internal/region/eu_config.go](mdc:internal/region/eu_config.go): EU Related configs
- [internal/region/us_config.go](mdc:internal/region/us_config.go): US Related configs

## Key Features

1. Region Selection
- Default region: US
- Region switching via `choreo region [region-name]`
- Thread-safe region selection with mutex protection
- Region persistence across sessions

2. Environment Support
- Each region (US/EU) has dev/stage/prod environments
- Environment override support for developers
- Production environment for end users

3. Token Management
- Region-specific token storage
- Token validation per region
- Automatic re-login prompt when switching regions

## Usage Flow
1. User logs in (defaults to US region)
2. User can switch regions using `choreo region [US|EU]`
3. System checks for valid token in new region
4. If no valid token exists, prompts for login
5. All subsequent operations use region-specific endpoints
